  "hints": [
    "Split into the two possible parities of n.",
    "Each case ends with its own witness: (n² + 3n + 4) = 2·witness."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Case $n = 2k$: $n^2 + 3n + 4 = 4k^2 + 6k + 4 = 2(2k^2 + 3k + 2)$.",
    "Case $n = 2k + 1$: $n^2 + 3n + 4 = 4k^2 + 10k + 8 = 2(2k^2 + 5k + 4)$.",
    "Both are even, and every integer falls in one case, so $n^2 + 3n + 4$ is even. $\\blacksquare$"
  ],
